/target
Cargo.lock

# The upstream Material Symbols variable font: a BUILD INPUT to `fonts/msymbols.py`,
# not an artifact of this repo. Apache-2.0, (c) Google - `FONTS-LICENSE-APACHE.txt`
# is committed and is what records the provenance.
#
# `scripts/fetch-upstream-fonts.sh` fetches it, at a pinned commit and
# SHA-256, to `fonts/upstream/` (ignored below); this older path stays ignored.
#
# Uncommitted on purpose: 10.7 MB that only the bake consumes, in a subunit that is
# meant to stay liftable. `msymbols.py` verifies every already-shipped icon against
# it outline-for-outline, so a wrong or moved upstream aborts the run rather than
# silently producing a face built half from one build and half from another.
fonts/MaterialSymbolsOutlined*.ttf

# The upstream faces: BUILD INPUTS to `fonts/*.py`, fetched with SHA-256
# checks by `scripts/fetch-upstream-fonts.sh` (the OFL faces from google/fonts
# at the commits named in `FONTS-LICENSE-OFL.txt`). Only the faces made from
# them (`fonts/*.ttf`) are committed.
fonts/upstream/

# Bake output: `scripts/bake-atlases.py` writes here and nowhere else, so a
# bake never dirties the tree. Committed copies are made from it deliberately.
/out/
